source: crates/standalone/fixture/src/lib.rs
---
Follow a build of this site to its end.

Usage: ink watch [OPTIONS] [BUILD]

Examples
  ink watch  # Follow the build that is running, or wait for the next

Arguments
  [BUILD]  The build to follow, by the start of its id. Without one, the build
           that is running or queued, or else the next one the site starts

Options
      --wait <SECONDS>  Seconds to wait before stopping; the build keeps going
                        on the server [default: 300]
      --poll <MS>       Milliseconds between two looks at the site
                        [default: 1000]

Account
      --api <URL>          The API's address, `http://host[:port]`;
                           `account.api` in the config file [env: INK_API]
      --site <ID>          The site's id; `account.site` in the config file
                           [env: INK_SITE]
      --org <ID>           Act as this organization, by its id: the site is one
                           of its sites, and the key's role there is what is
                           checked. See `ink org list` [env: INK_ORG]
      --timeout <SECONDS>  Seconds one call may take [default: 30]
                           [env: INK_TIMEOUT]
      --retries <N>        How many more times a call that is safe to repeat is
                           tried when the network fails [default: 2]
                           [env: INK_RETRIES]
      --retry-wait <MS>    Milliseconds before the first retry; each wait is
                           twice the one before [default: 500]
                           [env: INK_RETRY_WAIT]

Notes
  Follows a build to its end: the one named, the one running, or the next the
  site starts. Prints the deploy id.

Exit codes
  0  Done: the deploy is live
  1  The build was refused: the site does not build
  2  Wrong usage: the folder is linked to no site, or the folder cannot be read
  3  Not signed in, or the signature was refused
  4  The API could not be reached, the build failed or the wait ran out; safe to
     run again
  5  The deploy is recorded and not live, because publishing is paused after a
     rollback

Environment
  INK_API       The address of the API, as --api
  INK_SITE      The site's id, as --site
  INK_KEY       The private key to sign requests with, for a CI job; never a
                flag, so it stays out of process lists. `ink login` keeps one in
                the config folder instead
  INK_KEY_FILE  A file that holds that key, in place of INK_KEY

See also  ink push, ink status
Docs      https://github.com/uses-ink/uses.ink/blob/main/docs/cli.md
Global    -C, --json, -q, -v, --color, --no-progress, --log, --log-file
          (see `ink --help`)
